	(text "NOTES\n1. ACTIVE edge board (decision 0006): one per panel, edge code 0, 4-layer. The N-1 PASSIVE boards are a separate\n   2-layer design (hardware/edge-board-passive); shared parts keep the same references and footprints.\n2. Edge ID (R1, 1%) with D1 in series. V_ADC = Vf + (3.3V - Vf) * R_ID / (10k + R_ID), Vf(1N4148WS) ~0.45-0.6V:\n   code0 0R ~0.55V | code1 1k ~0.80V | code2 2k7 ~1.13V | code3 5k6 ~1.54V | code4 12k ~2.05V | code5 27k ~2.55V | idle 3.3V\n   Calibrate thresholds on hardware; D1 makes every SENSE->DRIVE path one-way so idle neighbours cannot form sneak paths.\n3. LED_RET: the last LED of the panel loops back through the last corner into J2 D_IN of the active board,\n   via the R7/R8 divider into PA6. Firmware counts returned bits (TIM3, TI1 ext. clock on PA6), 32 bits per LED.\n4. CAN termination: close JP1 only on the electrically farthest panel of a segment.\n5. Power: +12V enters via the bridge springs (J1 X2/X9) and corner joints; no 20 AWG crossover jumper is needed\n   because all contact pads sit on the exterior (power-plane) face at the wall edge. The +5V LED rail is made per\n   panel by U5 on the active board and runs around the panel through the corner joints; it never crosses a bridge." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15 228.6 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "a7d5ec9f-7318-4d40-bbc1-12160dc406a9"))
	(sheet_instances
		(path "/" (page "1"))
	)
	(embedded_fonts no)
)
